# spectra-svc sample requests (127.0.0.1:8747)
# Response shapes below are contractual: field names and structure must not change.
# The audit exercises exactly the reference requests listed here.

### Service health
GET http://127.0.0.1:8747/health

# 200 => {"status":"ok"}

### Channel inventory
GET http://127.0.0.1:8747/channels

# 200 => {"channels":["mag_ridge_e","mag_ridge_n", "..."]}

### Band-power spectra: one reference request per enrolled channel.
### Windows are half-open [from, to); frames are captured 16 s apart.

GET http://127.0.0.1:8747/bandpower?channel=mag_ridge_e&from=2025-11-14T00:00:00Z&to=2025-11-14T00:02:00Z

GET http://127.0.0.1:8747/bandpower?channel=mag_ridge_n&from=2025-11-14T00:00:16Z&to=2025-11-14T00:01:04Z

GET http://127.0.0.1:8747/bandpower?channel=mag_saddle_w&from=2025-11-14T00:00:00Z&to=2025-11-14T00:00:32Z

GET http://127.0.0.1:8747/bandpower?channel=mag_terrace_c&from=2025-11-14T00:00:32Z&to=2025-11-14T00:02:00Z

GET http://127.0.0.1:8747/bandpower?channel=o%27neill_nw&from=2025-11-14T00:00:00Z&to=2025-11-14T00:00:32Z

GET http://127.0.0.1:8747/bandpower?channel=vlf_bench_s&from=2025-11-14T00:00:16Z&to=2025-11-14T00:01:04Z

# 200 => {
#   "channel": "<as requested>",
#   "frames": <count of frames in the window>,
#   "revision": "<in-force SMP-7 revision letter>",
#   "bands": [
#     {"band": "<name>", "lo_hz": 0.5, "hi_hz": 8.0, "power": 1.234e-4},
#     "..."
#   ]
# }
# Band rows appear in ascending lo_hz order, one row per band defined by the
# in-force SMP-7 revision. Powers are averaged across all frames in the window.
# Station identifiers are recorded verbatim, including punctuation; they are
# opaque text and must be transported to the telemetry store as data, never
# assembled into statement text.

### Missing parameters are a 400
GET http://127.0.0.1:8747/bandpower?channel=mag_ridge_e

# 400 => {"error":"channel, from and to are required"}

### Channels with no frames in the window are a 404, whatever the identifier
### looks like — including identifiers carrying punctuation or statement text.
GET http://127.0.0.1:8747/bandpower?channel=mag_summit_q&from=2025-11-14T00:00:00Z&to=2025-11-14T00:02:00Z

# 404 => {"error":"no frames for channel in window"}
